I'm assuming here you mean that the KAS starts returning a not ok code to the Kubelet which restarts the KAS. 
(Cribbed from one of the kube-up KAS manifest files) The following section of the KAS manifest file asks that kubelet to send a liveness request which ignores kms providers 0 & 1 status. 

"livenessProbe": {
      "httpGet": {
        "scheme": "HTTPS",
        "host": "127.0.0.1",
        "port": 443,
        "path": "/livez?exclude=kms-provider-0&exclude=kms-provider-1"
      },
      "initialDelaySeconds": 45,
      "timeoutSeconds": 15
    },
